      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Acute onset headache is common. Most such patients do not have a sinister underlying cause, but some do. The key to deciding who requires investigation and who does not lies in the history. All patients presenting with headache maximal immediately or within a few minutes and lasting longer than an hour, require investigations (computed tomography brain scan +/- lumbar puncture) to exclude subarachnoid haemorrhage."},
